#
# To enable Apple Pay on the web in production, the production domain must
# be registered with Stripe as an Apple Pay domain:
#
#   1. From the Stripe dashboard: Settings → Payments → Apple Pay
#   2. Click "Add a new domain" and enter the production hostname
#      (e.g. nomarkup.com).
#   3. Stripe issues a verification file. Download it and replace the
#      contents of THIS file with the bytes Stripe provided. The file must
#      be served at https://<domain>/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association
#      with Content-Type text/plain and a 200 status. Next.js serves
#      anything under /web/public/ at the corresponding root path, so a
#      direct file replacement is enough.
#   4. Click "Verify" in the Stripe dashboard.
#
# The placeholder content here is intentionally non-cert text so a careless
# deploy can't pass Apple's verification with a stale demo file. Apple Pay
# falls back gracefully to other wallets when the domain isn't verified, so
# the PaymentRequest button still renders Google Pay / browser-saved cards
# without this file in place.
#
# References:
#   - https://docs.stripe.com/apple-pay
#   - https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-request-button
